ecting me. He's smart, brave and knows his stuff. His first priority was always what was best for Cassie. I thought the romance between them felt believable--not rushed. I felt for Cassie when she had to face her fear of heights because I'm afraid of heights too.<br /><br />I liked the way the author balanced the budding romance between Cassie and Levi with the action. I thought the plot moved at a steady pace until the exciting conclusion. I got so caught up reading I didn't want to put the book down to do other things. There never seemed to be a good place to stop reading. This is a great addition to my Traci Hunter Abramson book collection.<br /><br />I received a complimentary copy. All opinions expressed in this review are my own. I loved the book so much I bought a copy for my personal collection.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/55704599?shelf=arc-or-for-review" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">arc-or-for-review</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/55704599?shelf=book-launch" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">book-launch</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">8 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">2 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-