0.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3182625246">February 29, 2020</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">The following is my honest review of an advanced copy I was given of Royal Heir by Traci Hunter Abramson:<br /><br />I’ve been waiting a really long time to read this book. Ever since I read the author’s Royal series which includes Royal Target, Royal Secrets, and Royal Brides I’ve been wanting to see the character Levi Marin get his own happily ever after story. Traci has finally made my desires happen and she did not disappoint me. In fact, according to the author, this book is going to be a start of a brand new world she is creating. I can’t wait to see what happens next.<br /><br />Though Royal Heir is a start of a new world, you still got to see some old friends in this book which made my heart happy. After all, you can’t have a royal book without the dashing Prince Garrett and the heroic Princess Janessa of Meridia.<br /><br />This book is full of adventure, suspense, and some romance. All three great elements to make a great read. You are going to fall in love all over again as you get to know Levi Marin and Princess Cassandra (Cassie) of Sereno. You will not be disappointed with this read. I highly recommend this book to all suspense and romance readers.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--in