 romance part was throughout the book. You learn who the guilty party is near the beginning of the book but the mystery lies in why he committed the crime and how he will accomplish what he has set out to do.<br /><br />There are secrets and responsibilities that keep coming between Cassie and Levi's growing attraction. They are conflicted as to where their relationship is going to go, and Levi keeps trying to distance himself only to keep coming back not only because of his feelings but his sense of duty to protect Cassie.<br /><br />Traci knows how to write a suspense/mystery/romance and keep the reader reading. I started this book knowing that there were previous books in the series and there would be parts of the story that would be more familiar had I read the other books first. I found that while it would be nice to know that background story it wasn't necessary. <br /><br />It's a clean romance with a great mystery and suspense, it also shows great character development and conflict. I would recommend this novel to anyone who loves a great suspense with a wonderful love story. <br /><br />I was given access to an advanced copy, all opinions are my own.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">1 like</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.035