.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined0small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined0small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7076668101">December 11, 2024</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I finished Royal Duty (Sept 2024) and realized I had missed this novel from March of 2020. I’m going to guess the Covid shutdown somehow made me not pay attention to a book from an author I enjoy. Princess Cassandra of Sereno (Cassie) survives an assassination attempt in her family palace. Her father, the King, sends her to a neighboring Mediterranean country for safety. She is staying in a secure Royal castle retreat. Levi Marin is head of security and it is his assignment to protect her at all costs. She thinks he is a native of Meridia but he is actually a very entrenched CIA agent. (The local ruling family knows his full identity.) A lot of action is happening. Banks are simultaneously being robbed across Europe and it all ties to an old treaty and the rules of succession for Sereno when the King dies. <br /><br />Cassie is of course a hard working Royal and gets her first taste of a less formal life at the castle. She poses as Levi’s girlfriend to the staff and security officers. And maybe the romance isn’t as pretend as it seems. This is a really nice balance of action, and romance. I’m glad I realized I’d missed a book and was able to get it easily at my local library. I did notice that the lead in the next book which was just published makes an appearance at the end of this one. I marvel that the author can keep track of her various series when for example in this case it took four years for the next book.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/1401537?shelf=2024" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">2024</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/1401537?shelf=books-in-a-series-mysteries" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">books-in-a-series-mysteries</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/1401537?shelf=books-in-a-series-romance" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">books-in-a-series-romance</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></button></div></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">2 likes</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60