auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I’m so happy that Levi got his own Royals book. Cassie and Levi’s story was quite different from the previous books in the series for multiple reasons, all of which made for a new and suspense filled story. I also liked that we still saw some of our favorite characters from the previous books even while new characters were added and a new Royal line set up to follow. One of the questions I have is regarding CIA protocol and why Levi was almost always contacted by the director, is it because of his position, his role, or is that just the way it is. I’m pretty sure that’s going to be a question that’s never answered, but it’s there. Cassie seems a bit more rigid in her demeanor and attitude than the royals in Meiridia, but as the book progresses you see her change and realize that while her way worked, being more friends and/family with her staff was a way that she could change. I really liked the romance between Cassie and Levi. While it happened very quickly, they did spend a lot of time together, learning about each other and their lives. </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/132382878?shelf=read-in-2026" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">read-in-2026</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.0354193